<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoInputCreate</function></refname>
  <refpurpose></refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Input.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoInput *SilikoInputCreate(
	const struct SilikoInputVTable *source_table,
	void *source_state);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoInputCreate</function> function creates a
  <type>SilikoInput</type> objecr with
  <varname>source_table</varname> as its
  <type>SilikoInputVTable</type> and
  <varname>source_state</varname> as its state object.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoInputCreate</function> returns a pointer
to the newly created object if successful, or <literal>NULL</literal>
if there is an error. If <function>SilikoInputCreate</function>
returns a valid pointer, then the object must be passed to
<function>SilikoInputDestroy</function> to avoid a memory leak,
and <varname>source_state</varname> will be cleaned up when the object
is passed to <function>SilikoInputDestroy</function>. If
<function>SilikoInputCreate</function> returns
<literal>NULL</literal>, then the calling context is still responsible
for cleaning up <varname>source_state</varname>.</para>
</refsection>
